cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LS-BDD: a log-structured block device driver for research"
abstract: >-
  LS-BDD is a software-defined-storage block device driver for the Linux
  kernel, made for research. It implements log-structured storage, in which
  the logical block address translation table is a pluggable data structure
  (skip list, hash table, B+-tree, red-black tree; lock-free and blocking
  variants), together with a test system that automates the whole experiment
  cycle: declarative experiment descriptions, repeated fio runs and a
  statistical report.
authors:
  - given-names: Mikhail
    family-names: Gavrilenko
    alias: qrutyy
repository-code: "https://github.com/qrutyy/ls-bdd"
license: GPL-2.0-only
keywords:
  - log-structured storage
  - block device
  - Linux kernel
  - address translation table
  - lock-free data structures
  - performance evaluation
